## 13. Recommended decision rights

| Decision | Primary owner | Required challenge or approval |
|---|---|---|
| Whether to participate | Market leadership | Local cultural panel and regional brand |
| Cultural insight | Local strategy lead | Community advisers |
| Global platform fit | Regional/global brand | Market team |
| Language and terminology | Native-language lead | Independent native reviewer |
| Religious representation | Market owner | Multiple faith/cultural advisers |
| Product and dietary claims | Product/legal team | Certification specialist |
| Charity claims | Corporate affairs/legal | Community partner and finance |
| Final creative | Market lead | Cultural panel; global council for high-risk work |
| Creator content | Creator lead | Local claims and cultural review |
| Media timing | Market media lead | Local public affairs |
| Campaign pause | Market incident lead | Immediate authority without executive delay |
| Permanent withdrawal/apology | Market and global communications | Legal, cultural advisers, executive sponsor |

Local leaders should have authority to pause content immediately. They should not need to wait for headquarters while an issue spreads.

