## Key decisions

| Issue | Recommended posture |
|---|---|
| Global versus local | Global conduct standards with local authorship and authority |
| Regional Ramadan campaign | Use only where a genuine shared insight exists; otherwise create market or subregional chapters |
| Sacred practices | Represent only when necessary, accurate, and independently reviewed |
| Cultural advisers | Multiple paid advisers with meaningful challenge and escalation rights |
| Translation | Native transcreation plus independent review |
| Product role | Practical and truthful, not artificially inserted |
| Charity | Transparent, auditable, and not dependent on exploitative storytelling |
| Agencies | Common standards, local expertise, documented accountability |
| Creators | Partners in interpretation, not tokens or universal community spokespeople |
| AI-generated culture | Heavily restricted and always subject to expert review |
| Geotargeting | Never treated as protection from global scrutiny |
| Campaign approval | Risk-tiered review of the final asset and operational experience |
| Crisis response | Local pause authority with coordinated global escalation |
| Success | Trust, accuracy, reciprocity, and operational delivery alongside commercial performance |

## Conclusion

Authenticity should be treated as an operating discipline, not a creative style. It comes from **local authority, cultural specificity, community participation, accurate products and claims, reciprocal benefit, and willingness to correct mistakes**.

The brand should not seek one globally uniform expression of Ramadan, Lunar New Year, Diwali, or any other observance. It should instead maintain a consistent ethical standard while allowing communities to shape how—and whether—the brand participates.

Because every campaign is now globally visible, local authenticity and cross-border preparedness are not competing objectives. The strongest local work will be specific enough to feel true at home, while documented and contextualized well enough to withstand scrutiny anywhere.
